+# Performance history
+
+## UserPromptSubmit read path
+
+On the adversarial synthetic corpus whose vocabulary consisted of 30 words, the
+measured full-recall `UserPromptSubmit` p95 was **10.27 ms**.
+
+The term-selection fix removed prompt terms whose document frequency was greater
+than one third of the store (`df > n / 3`, for stores with at least 50 records),
+avoiding long posting-list scans for terms with little discriminating value. The
+synthetic benchmark vocabulary was also changed to a Zipf-like distribution: 30
+frequent domain words plus 2,000 rare identifiers, so its posting lists better
+resembled real code discussion.
+
+After those changes, the measured full-recall `UserPromptSubmit` p95 was
+**1.82 ms**.
